      "value": "@{680f1496b78da8b5132f3f14|full_name} I've confirmed that the issue you are seeing is from the fresnel effect. At shallow angles, objects become more specular, even if they started out fully diffuse. This is physically accurate.\n\nI see however that this makes editing a model that is supposed to be specular in some places, and entirely diffuse in others, challenging (until the upcoming avatar optimizer allows you to just use different materials). I'll see if there is some mostly-accurate way to scale the fresnel effect itself by the gloss map too.",
